# Prog 3: a Scrubbly (11x11 pixels), left column A, top row C.
# It is left-right symmetric, so only columns 0-5 are stored (three per
# number) and the renderer mirrors them: E = 2A+10 puts the mirror
# axis on the centre column. The main program sets W=3 and H=11.
2A+10→E:6733242712→D:Prog 4:2425542362→D:Prog 4
